<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Beylik of Mani</h1><p class="st-meta">1776 CE – 1821 CE · capital Limeni</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Semi-autonomous Ottoman principality of the Mani peninsula, whose last bey, Petrobey Mavromichalis, helped launch the Greek War of Independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maniots">Maniots</a> of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> had always resisted Ottoman control. After the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orlov-revolt">Orlov revolt</a> of 1770 and the Russo-Turkish peace of 1774, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> gave up direct rule and in 1776 created a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> under the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapudan-pasha">Kapudan Pasha</a>, the Ottoman admiral, with a Maniot bey.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The bey, chosen from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maniots">Maniot</a> clans, paid a modest tribute and kept order, but power remained with the feuding chieftain families in their stone tower houses. Notable beys included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tzanetos-grigorakis">Tzanetos Grigorakis</a> and, from 1815, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobey-mavromichalis">Petros Mavromichalis</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> was poor, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a>, piracy and a strong warrior tradition shaping its society.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In March 1821 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobey-mavromichalis">Petrobey Mavromichalis</a> declared revolt at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/areopolis">Areopolis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalamata">Kalamata</a>, joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> ended, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-hellenic-republic">First Hellenic Republic</a>, though its clans long resisted central government.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1776 CE – 1821 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.04%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1776 CE – 1821 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Limeni</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tzanetos Grigorakis, Petros Mavromichalis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Maniot Beylik, Mani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=beylik-of-mani" aria-label="Beylik of Mani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5242 855 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Beylik of Mani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5562 1111L5709 970M5562 1111L5570 1082"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5570 1082h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5562 1111h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5562 1111h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Limeni. <a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=beylik-of-mani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
